{title: Jingle Bells}
{artist: James Lord Pierpont, 1857}
{key: G}
{tempo: 120}
{difficulty: intermediate}
{tags: holiday, kids}

{start_of_verse: Verse}
[G]Dashing through the snow
In a [C]one-horse open sleigh
O'er the [D]fields we go
[D7]Laughing all the [G]way
Bells on bobtail ring
Making [C]spirits bright
What [Am]fun it is to [D]ride and sing
A sleighing song to[G]night[D]

{start_of_chorus}
[G]Jingle bells, jingle bells
Jingle all the way
[C]Oh what fun it [G]is to ride
In a [A7]one-horse open [D]sleigh, hey![D7]
[G]Jingle bells, jingle bells
Jingle all the way
[C]Oh what fun it [G]is to ride
In a [D]one-horse open [G]sleigh
